    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.extra\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, on `nvim v0.11.0-dev-1623+g34d808b73c` for some unknown reason `mini.extra`'s LSP picker doesn't use `mini.pick` when launched with scope `document_symbol`. It uses `loclist` instead.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nRepro config:\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\n\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({})\nrequire(\"mini.extra\").setup({})\n\nMiniDeps.add(\"neovim/nvim-lspconfig\")\n-- Needs `lua-language-server`\nrequire(\"lspconfig\").lua_ls.setup({})\n```\n\n1. Open any Lua file\n2. Do `:Pick lsp scope='document_symbol'`\n3. It uses loclist instead of `mini.pick`",
